  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2009-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Note that \\(a + b + c = f(1).\\)\n\nUsing \\(f(x + 3) = 3x^2 + 7x + 4\\) with \\(x = -2\\) gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} f(1) &= f(-2 + 3) \\\\ &= 3(-2)^2 + 7(-2) + 4 \\\\ &= 12 - 14 + 4 = 2. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "\\(a + b + c = f(1)\\)",
        "Write \\(1 = (-2) + 3\\) and use the given formula for \\(f(x + 3)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
